 "is_vocab": false,
 "stimulus_html": "Assume the conditional statement <span data-math=\"p \\to q:\">p \\to q:</span> “If my friend lives in San Francisco, then my friend does not live in California” is false, and use it to answer the following questions.",
 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 497487,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Write the converse of the statement in words and determine its truth value.",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>The converse of <span data-math=\"p \\rightarrow q\"></span> is <span data-math=\"q \\rightarrow p\"></span>.</p>\n<p>The original statement is “If my friend lives in San Francisco, then my friend does not live in California.</p>\n<p>The converse switches the position.</p>\n<p>Converse in words: If my friend does not live in California, then my friend lives in San Francisco.</p>\n<p>A conditional is only false if the premise is true, and the conclusion is false.</p>\n<p>For the original conditional statement <span data-math=\"p \\rightarrow q\"></span> to be false, you know that <span data-math=\"p\"></span> is true, and <span data-math=\"q\"></span> is false.</p>\n<p>Now consider the converse, <span data-math=\"q \\rightarrow p\"></span>. The premise, <span data-math=\"q\"></span>, is false, so the converse is true.</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "If my friend does not live in California, then my friend lives in San Francisco. True."
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  },
  {
   "id": 497488,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Write the inverse of the statement in words and determine its truth value.",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>The inverse of <span data-math=\"p \\rightarrow q\"></span> is <span data-math=\"{\\sim}p \\rightarrow {\\sim}q\"></span>.</p>\n<p>The original statement is “If my friend lives in San Francisco, then my friend does not live in California.</p>\n<p>The inverse negates each part without changing the order.</p>\n<p>Inverse in words: If my friend does not live in San Francisco, then my friend lives in California.</p>\n<p>A conditional is only false if the premise is true, and the conclusion is false.</p>\n<p>For the original conditional statement <span data-math=\"p \\rightarrow q\"></span> to be false, you know that <span data-math=\"p\"></span> is true, and <span data-math=\"q\"></span> is false.</p>\n<p>Now consider the inverse, <span data-math=\"{\\sim}p \\rightarrow {\\sim}q\"></span>. The premise, <span data-math=\"{\\sim}p\"></span>, is false, so the inverse is true.</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "If my friend does not live in San Francisco, then my friend lives in California. True."
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  },
  {
   "id": 497489,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Write the contrapositive of the statement in words and determine its truth value.",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>The contrapositive of <span data-math=\"p \\rightarrow q\"></span> is <span data-math=\"{\\sim}q \\rightarrow {\\sim}p\"></span>.</p>\n<p>The original statement is “If my friend lives in San Francisco, then my friend does not live in California.</p>\n<p>The contrapositive switches the position and negates each part.</p>\n<p>Contrapositive in words: If my friend lives in California, then my friend does not live in San Francisco.</p>\n<p>A conditional is only false if the premise is true, and the conclusion is false.</p>\n<p>For the original conditional statement <span data-math=\"p \\rightarrow q\"></span> to be false, you know that <span data-math=\"p\"></span> is true, and <span data-math=\"q\"></span> is false.</p>\n<p>Now consider the contrapositive, <span data-math=\"{\\sim}q \\rightarrow {\\sim}p\"></span>. The premise, <span data-math=\"{\\sim}q\"></span>, is true and the conclusion, <span data-math=\"{\\sim}p\"></span> is false. This makes the contrapositive false.</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "If my friend lives in California, then my friend does not live in San Francisco. False."
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
